    <tags>nexa-memkeeper memory optimizer ram tray windows rust portable</tags>
    <summary>Tray-resident memory optimizer for Windows — reclaims idle memory while staying under 5 MB itself.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
**Nexa MemKeeper** keeps an eye on Windows memory from the tray and reclaims what is
no longer needed. It is written in pure Rust on the Win32 API — no managed runtime,
no UI framework, no external DLLs beyond the OS inbox set.

### Highlights

* **Tiny by design** — under 1 MB on disk, idle working set around 1.5 MB.
  Feature code (process list, cleanup engine) runs in on-demand worker processes and
  is released the moment you close the window.
* **Top 5 popup** on tray click; **Task Manager-style process list** with app grouping,
  live search by name/PID/window title, and kill process / process tree / thread.
* **Cleanup areas you choose** — working-set trim, standby purges, modified-page flush,
  system working set, page combining. Each one can be switched off.
* **Automatic cleanup** on a usage threshold, on a schedule, or when Windows itself
  signals low memory — with a cooldown so it never thrashes.
* English/Korean UI.

### Notes

* This package installs the machine-wide (all users) build via the official installer
  downloaded from the project's GitHub Releases.
* Settings live next to the exe under `data\settings.ini`, falling back to
  `%LOCALAPPDATA%\NexaMemKeeper` when the install directory is not writable.
  **Uninstalling keeps your settings** so a reinstall restores them.
* Autostart is **not** enabled by this package — turn it on from the tray menu when you
  want it (it writes a single `HKCU\...\Run` value, and turning it off removes that value).

### License

Nexa MemKeeper is released under the **PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0** — free for
personal and other noncommercial use. **Commercial use requires a separate paid license**
— see the [license](https://github.com/SosomLab/nexa-memkeeper/blob/main/LICENSE.md) for
how to get in touch.

Product home: https://sosomlab.com
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SosomLab/nexa-memkeeper/releases</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
